# mm.fs.fat

FAT12, FAT16, and FAT32 with long file names on a BlockDevice, mounted at a
prefix: the format removable media carry, so a USB drive or SD card a board
writes reads on any PC. mount answers Corrupt for a device holding no FAT
volume and writes nothing to it; format makes one, partitioned as a PC
expects, erasing what was there.

The Pico SDKs bind platform.pico.fs.fat, which runs FatFs compiled by the
Pico bridge. A program reaching mm.fs.fat is unavailable on a lane that binds
no provider; with none bound the fallback answers Unsupported. unmount
detaches only volumes this module attached.
